<title>USA: Montana 700 MW Colstrip unit resumes full power.</title>
<headline>Montana 700 MW Colstrip unit resumes full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 700 megawatt (MW) Colstrip coal-fired power unit 4 near Billings, Mont., resumed full power production over the weekend following a repair outage, a Montana Power Co spokesman said Monday.</p>
<p>The unit was shut Nov 16 for repairs to a heater gear box.</p>
<p>Colstrip's other units, two at 330 MW and another at 700 MW, were operating normally, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Montana Power is the operator of Colstrip unit 4.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
</text>
